    "title": "Man sentenced to prison, accused of smuggling drugs at Atlanta airport - NewsBreak",
    "text": "A Customs and Border Protection Officer was sentenced to prison after being accused of smuggling illegal drugs at Atlanta’s Hartsfield-Jackson International Airport. Atlanta U.S. Attorney Teddy Hertzberg says 45-year-old Ivan Beverhoudt was caught by a K-9 officer at the Atlanta airport with smuggling cocaine. Beverhoudt faces 20 years in prison, officials say. Van says his office will always prosecute those who abuse their law enforcement authority.",
